---
import { Icon } from "astro-icon/components";
import Base from "../../layouts/base.astro";
---

<Base title="Hello, world">
  <article>
    <h1>Hello, world</h1>
    <p class="meta">
      <Icon name="calendar" size={16} /> Published 2026-01-12
      &middot;
      <Icon name="heart" size={16} /> 12 likes
      &middot;
      <Icon name="check" size={16} /> Verified author
    </p>
    <p>
      This is <strong>UC3</strong> (see examples/PERSONA.md): a page where every
      content icon (<code>calendar</code>, <code>heart</code>, <code>check</code>)
      is used exactly once. View source and you'll find three plain inline
      <code>&lt;svg&gt;</code> elements down here, not a single
      <code>&lt;symbol&gt;</code>/<code>&lt;use&gt;</code> pair - sprinting a
      single-use icon would cost bytes, not save them, so the build correctly
      does nothing. The nav icons in the header/footer around this article
      are a different story: they repeat, so they <em>are</em> deduped.
      Nobody configured either outcome.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
